{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1025292-kupala","id":1025292,"title":"Kupala","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-01T22:04:05-08:00","id":1025292,"title":"Kupala","content":"I've never played Werewolf, but I'm familiar with the mechanics. I'm putting together a dark ages vampire game set in the Carpathian Mountains. One of the players wants to play a werewolf or kinfolk. Kupala is the dominant spirit of the area. Is there reference to it in Werewolf? Do any tribes get taught gifts by it? What sort of gifts is it appropriate to teach? How powerful is it among spirits?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3362-darkwaters","name":"Darkwaters","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3362_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-01T22:10:43-08:00","id":1025294,"title":"","content":"Kupala appears more in the Vampire mythos than in the Werewolf one. If it is a spirit, it would be one of the most powerful and dangerous Wyrm spirits in the world. The only Tribe that would likely have a relation to it would be the Black Spiral Dancers. Basically in Werewolf terms the Kupala would be Evil (capital E) and definitely not be something a werewolf should be getting gifts from.<br /> <br /> You might want to consider other powerful Gaian spirits that could be found there for your players. The Shadowlords are the dominant tribe in part of the world, their primary patron spirit is Grandfather Thunder and there are lots other spirits of animals and nature that can be found in that area.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 01-02-2017, 01:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-01T22:16:20-08:00","id":1025298,"title":"","content":"I think some Werewolf material did hint Kupala could be one of the bound uber-Banes, whose freedom could herald the Final Battle - but Kupala is intentionally flexible that way. DtF made it an Earthbound Demon for example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-01T22:21:56-08:00","id":1025301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1025292-kupala?p=1025294#post1025294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kupala appears more in the Vampire mythos than in the Werewolf one. If it is a spirit, it would be one of the most powerful and dangerous Wyrm spirits in the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Meh. Probably not beyond the Talons of the Wyrm or the like. If it's a statted-out Earthbound, or on par with one, then it's not even getting to Incarna status.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The only Tribe that would likely have a relation to it would be the Black Spiral Dancers. Basically in Werewolf terms the Kupala would be Evil (capital E) and definitely not be something a werewolf should be getting gifts from. </div> </div> </div>Probably, yeah.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You might want to consider other powerful Gaian spirits that could be found there for your players. The Shadowlords are the dominant tribe in part of the world, their primary patron spirit is Grandfather Thunder and there are lots other spirits of animals and nature that can be found in that area. </div> </div> </div>Overwhelmingly, I'd say.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-01T22:43:24-08:00","id":1025311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1025292-kupala?p=1025301#post1025301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Meh. Probably not beyond the Talons of the Wyrm or the like. If it's a statted-out Earthbound, or on par with one, then it's not even getting to Incarna status.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, I said that if it were a spirit, it would be one of the most powerful and dangerous ones in the world - I don't believe that any of the Wyrm's Talons are currently hanging out taking an active (or even semi-active) hand in the world the way the Kupala does. And of the Wyrm's various spirits I do know that are active on Earth, there aren't any I can think of to compare with how powerful the Kupala has been portrayed.<br /> <br /> You're right though that it could be an Earthbound or even something else and certainly its power level is up in the air. Still, I generally imagine that if it were free (and a spirit) looking at the Storm Eater would be a good idea for getting a baseline figure for the Kupala's strength and then likely taking up another couple of notches.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-01T23:03:05-08:00","id":1025315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1025292-kupala?p=1025301#post1025301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Meh. Probably not beyond the Talons of the Wyrm or the like. If it's a statted-out Earthbound, or on par with one, then it's not even getting to Incarna status.</div> </div> </div> </div>It being an Earthbound in the context of DtF does not mean it's meant to be limited to that powerlevel in a different game's context. It's something that's meant to adjust to the roughly equivalent role in the given metaphysics.<br /> <br /> It's been a while since I read the rules, but with enough worship to fuel them, can't an Earthbound be pretty cataclysmic in its Lores?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-01T23:20:12-08:00","id":1025318,"title":"","content":"Personally, if I were to use Kupala in a Werewolf game, it's a powerful bane bound into the earth. Seems fairly straightforward. I wouldn't put it at Incarna status. Spirits can be plenty powerful and not be at that level.<br /> <br /> Shadow Lords wouldn't have anything to do with it it. Spirals would work with it. <br /> <br /> If the player wanted a connection to it, then they're playing a Spiral.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-02T01:08:03-08:00","id":1025333,"title":"","content":"The Shadowlords were said to have bound a great evil, Kupala, in the Spine of the World (Carpathian Mountains) in Prehistory. Basically they left it up to you to decide how you want to do it. Demon, Bane, or Physical Ur-Wyrm beast that now communicates through spirits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-02T07:40:19-08:00","id":1025427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1025292-kupala?p=1025315#post1025315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It being an Earthbound in the context of DtF does not mean it's meant to be limited to that powerlevel in a different game's context. It's something that's meant to adjust to the roughly equivalent role in the given metaphysics.<br /> <br /> It's been a while since I read the rules, but with enough worship to fuel them, can't an Earthbound be pretty cataclysmic in its Lores?</div> </div> </div> </div>Dream Makers are excessively potent in spite of not being Incarna, with an Essence of 300 and the ability to reshape reality (albeit that's never been mechanically described, and their W20 writeup repeated all of their old, outdated Charms rather than describe that one vital Charm and streamline the rest), and spirits can have over 10 in Rage, Gnosis, and Willpower, so the upper limits of Werewolf's mechanically-described power level should not be underestimated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-02T08:17:24-08:00","id":1025445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1025292-kupala?p=1025315#post1025315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's been a while since I read the rules, but with enough worship to fuel them, can't an Earthbound be pretty cataclysmic in its Lores?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. Lore Mastery allows you to multiply some aspects - duration, range, number of targets (not power or damage) - of your evocations. It's 10x increase per extra point of Faith, and you can enhance each aspect of a given evocation, by up to your Lore Mastery. The example given is Belial increasing a storm's radius from 8 yards to 91 miles and it's length from 8 turns to two and three quarters days. (While doing 10 dice of lethal damage with lightning and the winds having 9 dice of strength.)<br /> They also have Earthbound Lores: Contamination, Chaos (the last power is called 'Hell on Earth') and Violation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 01-02-2017, 11:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T23:08:00-08:00","id":1026875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1025292-kupala?p=1025301#post1025301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Meh. Probably not beyond the Talons of the Wyrm or the like. If it's a statted-out Earthbound, or on par with one, then it's not even getting to Incarna status.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's described in several Vampire books as a demon-god, so I'd say Incarna is about right when translated into a Werewolf game, probably around the level of Totem Incarnae. Apparently it's the supreme spirit of the Carpathian Mountains, and echoes of its power are spread worldwide by the Sabbat (and, if certain books are correct, the Tremere as well).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T09:47:10-08:00","id":1027086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1025292-kupala?p=1026875#post1026875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's described in several Vampire books as a demon-god, so I'd say Incarna is about right when translated into a Werewolf game, probably around the level of Totem Incarnae. Apparently it's the supreme spirit of the Carpathian Mountains, and echoes of its power are spread worldwide by the Sabbat (and, if certain books are correct, the Tremere as well).</div> </div> </div> </div>What Vampire has to say about spirits tends to not necessarily sync up with what other games say about it. In fact, it probably won't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T10:06:04-08:00","id":1027730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1025292-kupala?p=1027086#post1027086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What Vampire has to say about spirits tends to not necessarily sync up with what other games say about it. In fact, it probably won't.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thing is, the OP is asking for ideas to work a Garou in a Vampire game.<br /> <br /> My suggestion is to first define what Kupala is <u>at your chronicle</u>. Since it is a Vampire game, Kupala is relevant for being a patron of sorts to the Tzimisce, though their relation with Kupala isn't simple. The &quot;demon&quot; taught them Koldunism, but most Kolduns worked to keep Kupala bound. Some have ideas and roles pretty similar to werewolves in the region.<br /> <br /> I would make Kupala an Incarnae, but actual power-level will probably be a lesser question. It is certainly a Bane, that is above any question. Even Demons are Banes from Werewolf perspective, at the end. Shadowlords are probable to have the most information on Kupala, though it is up to the ST to decide if currently the keeping of its prison is mainly on the hands of the Shadowlords or the Tzimisce. They won't have Kupala as totem, unless you hack Werewolf (it is an option). Dancers can serve Kupala, and since it isn't a Werewolf game, you can have a sympathetic enough one for your Vampire game. Otherwise, look for the Shadowlords book for an idea on the kind of spirits you'll find at the region.<br /> <br /> Even the Vampire books on the region can help when they deal with Koldunism. This Discipline deals with spirits in general, not only Kupala or its kin, so some of those spirits can be accessible for Garou without any problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T10:44:43-08:00","id":1027751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> but most Kolduns worked to keep Kupala bound. </div> </div> </div> As an aside, what books talk about this? Interested as a fan of Koldunism who hadn't heard that part before.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T12:51:04-08:00","id":1027808,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure, since I'm working from memory, so you should take it with a grain of salt. But I have a clear memory of this, or at least of some Kolduns not wanting to have anything to do with the demon. It does work as headcanon to me, if that matters at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}